The image shows a bar chart with three sets of data over a period from 2015 to 2021. The data is categorized into three groups: Stock Returns, Interest Rates, and Return-Rate Ratio. The source of the data is Bloomberg.

To convert this information into a nested Python dictionary, we would structure the data as follows:

